  "system": {
    "finalName": "",
    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Scum_and_Villainy\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy\">Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy</a></i> </p><p>This Pistol-sized Repeating Blaster, intended for use indoors and in close-quarters combat, is preferred by pirates and bounty hunters who want to carry a lot of firepower in a small package. </p><p>A Subrepeating Blaster is an <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Autofire\" title=\"Autofire\">Autofire</a>-only Weapon and includes a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Retractable_Stock\" title=\"Retractable Stock\">Retractable Stock</a>. Unless the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Retractable_Stock\" title=\"Retractable Stock\">Retractable Stock</a> is extended, you cannot <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Brace\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Brace\">Brace</a> before making an <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Autofire\" title=\"Autofire\">Autofire</a> attack. </p><p>A Subrepeating Blaster requires a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Power_Pack\" title=\"Power Pack\">Power Pack</a> to operate. After 50 shots, the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Power_Pack\" title=\"Power Pack\">Power Pack</a> must be replaced. </p>",
